{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nI am writing from Duxan, having stopped for the night. The road here is quiet, and the evening air is cool enough to make a man appreciate the warmth of our own parlor, where you are keeping the hearth bright for my return. I have been thinking of the little ones; do tell me how Karl and Immanuel fared this week, and that Ludwig is not causing too much mischief in the study.\n\nThe journey is steady, though the miles seem to stretch when one is away from familiar faces. I do miss our evening conversations, and the simple pleasure of a shared meal without the distraction of postillions and inns. I shall reach Töplitz by morning, I hope, where I intend to spend a day in rest before continuing. Do not worry over my health; I am as robust as ever, though perhaps a little stiff in the joints from the carriage.\n\nGive my love to all.\n\nYours ever,\nG.W.F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795219112,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":209,"prompt_tokens":895,"total_tokens":1104,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-j1QHModrwjcUQwfO4NzutybhEJchR0iE","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":895,"prompt_ms":914.53,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.0218212290502793,"prompt_per_second":978.6447683509562,"predicted_n":209,"predicted_ms":4904.409,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.578889423076923,"predicted_per_second":42.41081851044642}}